module v2.std.subject_evidence

import v2.std.logic { Bool }

// CLAIM-ENTAILING EVIDENCE. An evidence standing may establish a proposition P only when EVERY
// execution path that constructs that standing proves the subject reached the relevant phase AND
// entails P:
//
//     E(execution)  =>  subject_phase_reached(execution)  AND  P(execution)
//
// The quantifier is the whole content. One path that constructs the standing without the subject
// having run invalidates the evidence, however sound every other path is.
//
// TWO MECHANICALLY DIFFERENT VIOLATIONS THIS CARRIER CLOSES, and they need different eyes -- a
// search that finds one will not find the other.
//
//   A. OUTCOME COLLAPSE. A coproduct with distinct causes folded to one Bool. The tell is a
//      discarded payload on a non-pass arm: `BuildFailed { diagnostic: _ } => false` throws away
//      the fact that decides whether the assertion EXECUTED, and a semantic counterexample then
//      shares one value with a comparison that never happened.
//
//   B. PREDICATE CAUSE ALIASING. No coproduct, nothing discarded, still invalid. `run.success ==
//      false` is true when a planted fault was detected AND when the binary never existed, the
//      process never spawned, or the host failed. The predicate's truth set is simply wider than
//      the proposition it is cited to prove.
//
//   B is why a lens over discarded payloads is insufficient as the remedy: A collapses a coproduct,
//   B never had one. Construction is what closes both -- there is no spelling of this type in which
//   a transport observation inhabits the completed arm.
//
// RULED INSUFFICIENT AS EVIDENCE, and named here so the list is reachable from the carrier rather
// than only from a message: `run.success == false`, `exit_code != 0`, `output absent`. These are
// TRANSPORT OBSERVATIONS. They report on the pipe, not on the subject.
//
// WHY THE OUTER SPLIT IS OWNER-SHAPED RATHER THAN PHASE-SHAPED. The two no-verdict arms differ in
// WHOSE deficit produced the absence, which is the distinction that decides who repairs it:
// EvidenceInstrumentRefused is the harness failing to pose the question at all (a fixture that
// would not construct, a probe whose subject could not be assembled); EvidenceSubjectUnreached is
// the instrument working correctly and the SUBJECT not arriving at the phase the claim is about.
// gunbc.emit_subject_clean_frontier made exactly this correction on its own side when every
// unreached measurement was rendering as `PopulationUnproduced` -- asserting the emitter produced
// nothing, when for a talkative subject the emitter produced a population perfectly well and the
// READER's buffer was too small. Collapsing the two arms here would re-open that defect one level up.
//
// WHY THE CAUSE IS A TYPE PARAMETER AND NOT A FIELD PAIR. The ruling asks a no-verdict standing to
// name the EXACT phase and cause. A `{ phase, cause }` record admits a phase from one stage beside a
// cause from another -- the states are independently writable, so nothing stops a Build phase
// carrying a Run diagnostic. Handing the consumer ONE type that names both makes the mismatch
// unrepresentable rather than merely wrong (DESIGN 4b: construction over validation). It is also
// what keeps this from becoming the giant universal error enum the ruling forbids: each consumer
// supplies its own closed vocabulary, so a new phase in one consumer is invisible to every other.
//
// WHAT THIS TYPE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: it carries no verdict of its own. Whether a completed
// outcome LICENSES a claim is the domain's question, answered by the domain's own outcome type, and
// folding the two would make one carrier answer for two authorities.
type SubjectEvidence<NoVerdict, Outcome>
  = EvidenceInstrumentRefused { cause: NoVerdict }
  | EvidenceSubjectUnreached { cause: NoVerdict }
  | EvidenceSubjectCompleted { outcome: Outcome }

// THE COMPARISON OUTCOME, kept as a SEPARATE type from the standing above rather than as three flat
// variants beside it. That separation is what makes one standing shape serve both an equivalence
// comparison and a fault-injection detection: the standing answers `did the subject run`, the
// outcome answers `and what did it say`. Fusing them would mint a second standing per domain.
//
// BehaviorDivergent CARRIES ITS DIFFERENCE. A divergence with no recoverable difference is a Bool
// wearing a variant's name, and the difference is free at the point of construction and
// unrecoverable afterwards.
//
// BehaviorEquivalent CARRIES NOTHING, and that is a deliberate refusal rather than an omission. The
// obvious symmetry would give it a `receipt` field, but the producers that exist have no receipt to
// put there -- `v2.std.verdict` `Pass` is a payload-free variant -- so the field would be filled
// with a placeholder at every construction site. A receipt nobody produced is the fabricated
// plausible output this repository forbids, and it is worse here than elsewhere because the whole
// point of this module is that a carrier must not be able to assert what was never observed. A
// later consumer that genuinely holds an agreement receipt adds the parameter then, with a producer
// behind it.

type BehavioralComparison<Difference>
  = BehaviorEquivalent
  | BehaviorDivergent { difference: Difference }

// THE ONLY SANCTIONED PROJECTION TO Bool, and it exists so that the collapse happens at ONE audited
// site instead of once per consumer. A no-verdict standing answers `false` here -- not because
// false means the claim was refuted, but because a claim is not established by an execution that
// did not happen. Callers that need to distinguish the two match the coproduct directly; this is
// for the terminal `test fn` boundary, which can only return Bool.
fn subject_evidence_establishes<NoVerdict, Outcome>(
  evidence: SubjectEvidence<NoVerdict, Outcome>,
  licenses: fn(Outcome) -> Bool
) -> Bool {
  match evidence {
    EvidenceSubjectCompleted { outcome: o } => licenses(o)
    EvidenceInstrumentRefused { cause: _ } => false
    EvidenceSubjectUnreached { cause: _ } => false
  }
}

// THE CAUSE-SWAP DISCRIMINATOR. This is what a control asserts against, and it is deliberately NOT
// the negation of the function above. `subject_evidence_establishes` answering false is satisfied
// by a genuine refutation AND by an execution that never happened -- the very aliasing this module
// exists to remove, so a control written against it would prove nothing. This answers the narrower
// question the control actually needs: was a verdict produced at all.
fn subject_evidence_produced_a_verdict<NoVerdict, Outcome>(
  evidence: SubjectEvidence<NoVerdict, Outcome>
) -> Bool {
  match evidence {
    EvidenceSubjectCompleted { outcome: _ } => true
    EvidenceInstrumentRefused { cause: _ } => false
    EvidenceSubjectUnreached { cause: _ } => false
  }
}
